How Is It Corrected or Treated?
Astigmatism does not heal on its own, but it can easily be corrected:
1. Eyeglasses
The simplest and safest option. Lenses are built with a cylindrical correction to compensate for the uneven curve of the eye.
2. Contact Lenses
Toric Lenses: Soft contact lenses specifically designed for astigmatism. They have different powers in different meridians and are weighted so they don't rotate when you blink.
Rigid Gas Permeable (RGP) Lenses: Hard contacts that provide a smooth, firm new optical surface over an irregular cornea. Ideal for higher or irregular astigmatism.
3. Refractive Surgery (Laser Correction)
For those looking for a permanent solution (typically for individuals over 18 with a stable prescription):
LASIK / PRK / SMILE: Lasers reshape the corneal tissue to make it smooth and symmetrical.
